Article 4 The compilation of legal regulations shall comply with the following division of responsibilities:
(1) Compilations of laws shall be compiled by the Legislative Affairs Commission of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress;
(2) Compilations of administrative regulations shall be compiled by the Ministry of Justice;
(3) Compilations of military regulations shall be compiled by the Legal Affairs Bureau of the Central Military Commission;
(4) Compilations of departmental rules shall be compiled by the respective departments of the State Council in accordance with their scope of functions;
(5) Compilations of local regulations and local government rules shall be compiled by the institutions designated by the local people's congresses and their standing committees and the local people's governments that have the authority to formulate local regulations and local government rules.
The Legislative Affairs Commission of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress and the Ministry of Justice may compile comprehensive compilations of laws, administrative regulations, departmental rules, local regulations, and local government rules; the Legal Affairs Bureau of the Central Military Commission may compile compilations of military-related laws, regulations, and orders; the departments of the State Council may, in accordance with their scope of functions, compile specialized compilations of laws, administrative regulations, and departmental rules; the local people's congresses and their standing committees and the local people's governments that have the authority to formulate local regulations and local government rules may compile compilations of local regulations and local government rules formulated in their respective regions.

Article 7 For the publication of compilations of legal regulations, the national administrative department of publishing shall, in accordance with the principles of professional division of labor in publishing, examine and approve in accordance with the following division of responsibilities:
(1) Compilations of laws shall be published by a central-level publishing house selected by the Legislative Affairs Commission of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress;
(2) Compilations of administrative regulations shall be published by a central-level publishing house selected by the Ministry of Justice;
(3) Compilations of military regulations shall be published by a central-level publishing house selected by the Legal Affairs Bureau of the Central Military Commission;
(4) Compilations of departmental rules shall be published by a central-level publishing house selected by the respective departments of the State Council;
(5) Compilations of local regulations and local government rules shall be published by a central-level publishing house or a local publishing house selected by the local people's congresses and their standing committees and the local people's governments that have the authority to formulate local regulations and local government rules.

Article 13 Anyone who violates these Provisions and publishes a compilation of legal regulations without authorization may, depending on the circumstances, be subject to the following administrative penalties by the administrative department of publishing or the administrative department for industry and commerce in accordance with the division of their functions:
(1) a warning;
(2) cessation of sale;
(3) confiscation or destruction;
(4) confiscation of illegal income;
(5) a fine;
(6) suspension of business for rectification;
(7) cancellation of the registration of the publishing house;
(8) revocation of the business license.
